WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.350
Step ten puts every owner,
cadence and test in one place.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.702
The cadence is design guidance: weekly,
rerun the exposure register; monthly,

3
00:00:09.702 --> 00:00:15.138
the policy compliance export, exemptions
due, and false positives; quarterly,

4
00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:20.490
DDoS coverage and cost, firewall rules,
vault access and the rule-set version;

5
00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.227
twice a year, a Front Door
failover and a vault restore;

6
00:00:24.227 --> 00:00:28.050
and yearly, a DDoS simulation
with an approved partner.

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.638
In a DDoS attack, the alert
pages the security monitor,

8
00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:36.612
and under Network Protection a severity
A request goes to Rapid Response.

9
00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:40.774
The metrics measure protected
coverage, not whether a setting exists.

10
00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:45.537
And each step supports controls in
NIST special publication eight hundred

11
00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:49.468
fifty-three, such as denial-of-service
and boundary protection,

12
00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:53.625
with the fed-ramp twenty X key
security indicators as a vocabulary.

13
00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:57.310
The steps support those
controls; the assessor decides.
